---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Nav from "../components/landing/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "../components/landing/Footer.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;

const h2 = "mt-14 text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-950";
const p = "mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-neutral-700";
const a = "text-primary font-medium underline underline-offset-2";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy — Kampa"
  description="Kampa runs entirely in your browser. No accounts, no analytics, no servers storing your data."
>
  <Nav />

  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-16 pb-24">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-neutral-950">
      Privacy
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-neutral-500">
      What happens to your key, your answers, and your campaigns.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>The short version</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      We run no servers, create no accounts, and store nothing about you. There
      is no database with your name in it, because there is no database. The
      rest of this page explains what that means concretely.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Your API key</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      Your Anthropic API key stays in your browser. By default it lives in
      sessionStorage, which the browser clears when you close the tab. It moves
      to localStorage only if you tick <strong
        class="font-semibold text-neutral-950">remember on this device</strong
      >. Either way it never reaches us: the key is sent only to
      api.anthropic.com over HTTPS, straight from your browser. Hitting <strong
        class="font-semibold text-neutral-950">Clear key</strong
      >
      removes it from storage.
    </p>
    <p class={p}>
      Create a spend-capped key anyway. It costs you nothing and puts a hard
      ceiling on any surprise. See the <a
        class={a}
        href={base + "guide/api-key"}>API key guide</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Your campaign data</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      The answers you type and the campaigns Kampa generates live in your
      browser's storage only. They are never uploaded to us. When you export a
      campaign, the file is downloaded to your machine like any other download.
      Clearing your browser storage deletes the lot, so export anything you want
      to keep.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>What Anthropic sees</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      Kampa sends your prompts to Anthropic's API to generate campaigns, so
      Anthropic processes that text under their own terms. Read <a
        class={a}
        href="https://www.anthropic.com/legal/privacy"
        rel="noopener">Anthropic's privacy policy</a
      > before you paste anything confidential.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>What we see</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      Nothing. No analytics, no cookies, no tracking pixels, no logs. The site
      is a folder of static files, and it has no code that reports back to us.
      Kampa is open source, so you can check that claim yourself instead of
      taking our word for it.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Hosting</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      Those static files are served by GitHub Pages. GitHub may log standard web
      requests, such as your IP address and browser, the way any web host does.
      That is between you and them: see the <a
        class={a}
        href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
        rel="noopener">GitHub Privacy Statement</a
      >.
    </p>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Base>
